 "requested_at": "2026-11-13T20:10:54.752510Z",
 "text": "No, this clause is not enforceable. \n\nThe clause attempts to authorize the common law remedy of distress (seizing and holding a tenant's personal property to compel payment of rent arrears). Under **section 40** of the *Residential Tenancies Act, 2006*, distress is abolished in residential tenancies: a landlord is strictly prohibited from seizing a tenant's property, without legal process, for default in the payment of rent or the breach of any other obligation. (Under section 4 of the Act, any lease provision that conflicts with this prohibition is void.)\n\nVerdict: not enforceable\nSection: 40",
